Chapter: PlugOracleArith

 Integer division and the two remainders are what this asks about, because
 that is where languages disagree silently rather than failing to compile.
 Codex `/` truncates toward zero, `int-rem` takes the sign of the dividend,
 and `int-mod` is Euclidean. Python, Ruby, Lua and Perl floor instead;
 Haskell's `div` floors where its `quot` truncates; Dart's `%` is never
 negative. Every one of those disagreements is invisible to a compile and
 invisible to a round trip through the same plug.

Section: Operations

  dv : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  dv (a) (b) = a / b

  rm : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rm (a) (b) = int-rem a b

  md : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  md (a) (b) = int-mod a b

Section: Bounded fields

 A clamping bounded field saturates at the declared band rather than
 wrapping or trapping. No target language does this natively: C#, Python
 and JavaScript all store what they are given, so the saturation has to
 be emitted by the plug from the field's declared type. That makes it the
 same class of silent disagreement as the remainders above -- a store
 that stops clamping compiles, runs, and answers 150 where the answer is
 100.

  Gauge = record {
    g : Integer between -100 and 100 clamping
  }

  gauge : Integer -> Integer
  gauge (n) = (Gauge { g = n }).g

Section: Report

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (show (dv 7 3))
   print-line-uni (show (dv (0 - 7) 3))
   print-line-uni (show (dv 7 (0 - 3)))
   print-line-uni (show (dv (0 - 7) (0 - 3)))
   print-line-uni (show (dv (0 - 9) 8))
   print-line-uni (show (dv (0 - 8) 8))
   print-line-uni (show (rm 7 3))
   print-line-uni (show (rm (0 - 7) 3))
   print-line-uni (show (rm 7 (0 - 3)))
   print-line-uni (show (rm (0 - 7) (0 - 3)))
   print-line-uni (show (rm (0 - 9) 8))
   print-line-uni (show (rm (0 - 8) 8))
   print-line-uni (show (md 7 3))
   print-line-uni (show (md (0 - 7) 3))
   print-line-uni (show (md 7 (0 - 3)))
   print-line-uni (show (md (0 - 7) (0 - 3)))
   print-line-uni (show (md (0 - 9) 8))
   print-line-uni (show (gauge 150))
   print-line-uni (show (gauge (0 - 150)))
   print-line-uni (show (gauge 42))
  end
